  "description": "Replacement of the existing flat roof to pitched roof, height of new roof 3.92m from eave level to ridge level, including additions of side dormers and roof lights, Double side storey extension and second floor loft conversion",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development would be sited within close proximity to a number of trees that are protected by virtue of them being sited within a conservation area and due to the lack of an appropriate tree survey and arboricultural impact assessment plan in accordance with best practice, the local planning authority is unable to fully assess the impacts of the proposed development on the retained trees and in the absence of such details the&amp;nbsp; proposal would therefore be contrary to Policy G14 of Harrow Local Plan 2021-2041 and policy G7 of the London Plan 2021.",
    "&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot;&gt;The proposed two storey side extension, alteration to\r\nfenestrations and roof alterations, by reason of its scale, inappropriate roof\r\nform, misaligned fenestrations would result&amp;nbsp; in an unduly, obtrusive and\r\nincongruous addition to the original dwellinghouse which would fail to respect\r\nthe character and proportions of the dwellinghouse, cause loss of\r\nopenness &amp;nbsp;and detrimentally impact the &amp;nbsp;visual amenity of the\r\nlocality and Conservation Area and harm setting of the nearby locally listed\r\nbuilding. There is not clear and convincing justification for the\r\nheritage harm that would result, nor public benefits to outweigh them. There\r\nis also insufficient detailed information to fully assess. Therefore the\r\nproposal would be contrary to the high quality design aspiration of the\r\nNational Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policy D3 (D.1 and D.11) and HC1 of\r\nThe London Plan (2021), Policies GR1 and HE1 of the Harrow Local Plan\r\n(2021-2041)and the relevant provisions of the Harrow Supplementary Planning\r\nDocument Residential Design Guide (2010).&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
